WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.361
- He was a philosopher, self-help author

00:00:02.361 --> 00:00:03.753
and motivational speaker.

00:00:03.753 --> 00:00:05.591
His first book, Your Erroneous Zones,

00:00:05.591 --> 00:00:08.010
is one of the best
selling books of all time.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.867
His message resonated with many

00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:12.255
in the new thought movement and beyond.

00:00:12.255 --> 00:00:14.030
He's Wayne Dyer and here's my take

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.943
on his Top 10 Rules to
Success, Volume Two.

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:19.008
Rule number three is my personal favorite.

00:00:19.008 --> 00:00:21.417
And I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:21.417 --> 00:00:22.855
And as always as you're watching,

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:25.111
if you hear something that
really resonates with you

00:00:25.111 --> 00:00:26.881
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:26.881 --> 00:00:28.389
put quotes around it so other people

00:00:28.389 --> 00:00:29.654
can be inspired as well.

00:00:29.654 --> 00:00:31.064
And when you write it down,

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.618
it's much more likely to
stick with you as well,

00:00:33.618 --> 00:00:34.451
Enjoy.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:40.970
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.985
- Creative visualization is
what we're talking about here.

00:00:49.985 --> 00:00:54.084
You, the imagery or
the image that you have

00:00:54.084 --> 00:00:56.831
of anything in your life is
really like mental behavior,

00:00:56.831 --> 00:00:58.227
it's like going out and practicing.

00:00:58.227 --> 00:00:59.668
If you go out and practice
with a basketball,

00:00:59.668 --> 00:01:02.041
shooting free-throws over and over again,

00:01:02.041 --> 00:01:03.759
that's physical practice.

00:01:03.759 --> 00:01:06.797
Imagery is mental practice,
it's mental behavior.

00:01:06.797 --> 00:01:09.796
When you have an image that
you can succeed at something,

00:01:09.796 --> 00:01:11.684
when you have an image that you can do it,

00:01:11.684 --> 00:01:12.994
rather than you can't do it.

00:01:12.994 --> 00:01:13.979
When you get into your car

00:01:13.979 --> 00:01:14.812
and you have an image

00:01:14.812 --> 00:01:16.312
that you're going to find a parking place,

00:01:16.312 --> 00:01:17.966
rather than there'll be no place to park,

00:01:17.966 --> 00:01:20.022
so you're not looking
for no place to park.

00:01:20.022 --> 00:01:22.471
You will start acting on
the image that you have,

00:01:22.471 --> 00:01:23.862
very much like you will start acting

00:01:23.862 --> 00:01:25.043
on the practice that you have

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:26.193
when you're shooting baskets

00:01:26.193 --> 00:01:27.674
or when you're hitting a forehand

00:01:27.674 --> 00:01:30.750
or working on your soup or
anything else that you're doing.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.789
The telling moment of my life

00:01:32.789 --> 00:01:35.488
occurred on the 30th of August, 1974

00:01:35.488 --> 00:01:38.085
when I went to my father's grave,

00:01:38.085 --> 00:01:41.142
after finding out he had
been dead for 10 years.

00:01:41.142 --> 00:01:43.562
And I went there with
a different intention

00:01:43.562 --> 00:01:46.230
on what I was going to do on his grave.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:48.030
I was so filled with rage and anger

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.280
and hatred toward this man.

00:01:51.196 --> 00:01:54.482
But rather than do what
I had gone there to do,

00:01:54.482 --> 00:01:58.649
something, some invisible,
divine, organizing intelligence,

00:01:59.925 --> 00:02:03.857
that moves the planets
and grows your fingernails

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.524
and beats your heart

00:02:07.614 --> 00:02:10.566
that commander in the command center

00:02:10.566 --> 00:02:12.210
to which you are always connected,

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.877
your, I am presence, if you will

00:02:15.982 --> 00:02:18.114
called me back to his grave

00:02:18.114 --> 00:02:22.281
after I cursed him for two
hours on that Friday afternoon.

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:30.822
And I stood there and I
said from this moment on

00:02:30.822 --> 00:02:32.155
I send you love.

00:02:34.068 --> 00:02:34.901
Who am I,

00:02:36.306 --> 00:02:38.722
who am I to judge you?

00:02:38.722 --> 00:02:41.298
You did what you knew how to do,

00:02:41.298 --> 00:02:44.453
given the conditions of your life.

00:02:44.453 --> 00:02:47.036
And when I left that grave site

00:02:48.082 --> 00:02:50.665
I was a completely changed man.

00:02:52.542 --> 00:02:56.422
Alcohol hasn't touched
my lips since that day.

00:02:56.422 --> 00:02:58.255
I walked away from it.

00:02:59.958 --> 00:03:02.090
I got myself into the
best shape of my life.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.938
I began running and

00:03:03.938 --> 00:03:06.194
relationships began to change.

00:03:06.194 --> 00:03:08.662
The right people, the right
woman came into my life,

00:03:08.662 --> 00:03:11.341
my children began to appear

00:03:11.341 --> 00:03:13.177
because when you advance confidently

00:03:13.177 --> 00:03:16.735
in the direction of your own dreams

00:03:16.735 --> 00:03:20.963
and endeavor to live the
life which you have imagined

00:03:20.963 --> 00:03:24.891
you will meet with a success
unexpected in common hours.

00:03:24.891 --> 00:03:26.650
Everything about my life changed.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.911
My writing took on a
whole different flavor.

00:03:28.911 --> 00:03:30.494
Before I was stuck,

00:03:32.025 --> 00:03:34.808
I checked into a motel
room, The Spindrift Motel,

00:03:34.808 --> 00:03:38.090
on A1A in Fort Lauderdale, Florida.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:39.862
Then I wrote a book that today

00:03:39.862 --> 00:03:43.885
has over 100 million copies
in print in 47 languages

00:03:43.885 --> 00:03:46.670
called Your Erroneous Zones.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:49.503
It came because the rage was gone.

00:03:51.112 --> 00:03:54.195
Mark Twain once said that forgiveness

00:03:55.656 --> 00:03:56.989
is the fragrance

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.530
that the violet sheds

00:04:02.668 --> 00:04:06.088
on the heal that has crushed it.

00:04:06.088 --> 00:04:07.970
That's divine love.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.423
My friend Byron Katie says that

00:04:10.423 --> 00:04:13.712
to believe that you
need what you don't have

00:04:13.712 --> 00:04:16.301
is the definition of insanity.

00:04:16.301 --> 00:04:19.908
To believe that you
need what you don't have

00:04:19.908 --> 00:04:23.096
because you're already here,
so you've already proven

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:24.822
that you don't need it.

00:04:24.822 --> 00:04:26.349
So to go around believing that

00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:28.607
I can't be happy, fulfilled,

00:04:28.607 --> 00:04:30.082
you know whatever it is,

00:04:30.082 --> 00:04:32.897
unless I get this stuff
that I don't already have

00:04:32.897 --> 00:04:34.255
it's a complete and total illusion,

00:04:34.255 --> 00:04:36.301
it's a thought that isn't even true,

00:04:36.301 --> 00:04:38.055
there's no truth to it whatsoever,

00:04:38.055 --> 00:04:41.178
you don't need anything
and when you get that

00:04:41.178 --> 00:04:42.908
the irony is you're no longer,

00:04:42.908 --> 00:04:44.795
you're no longer attached,

00:04:44.795 --> 00:04:48.921
your total life is just
about living those virtues.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.256
How can I serve, how can I be sincere,

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:54.169
how can I be gentle,
how can I be supportive?

00:04:54.169 --> 00:04:55.602
And thinking like that,

00:04:55.602 --> 00:04:58.435
and that's how I think
now and because of that

00:04:58.435 --> 00:04:59.652
I'm in meaning

00:04:59.652 --> 00:05:01.765
and being in meaning,

00:05:01.765 --> 00:05:05.064
the times that I was in ambition

00:05:05.064 --> 00:05:05.897
you know

00:05:09.058 --> 00:05:11.334
is delivering more and
more and more and more

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:14.044
of what I wanted so much then

00:05:14.044 --> 00:05:16.417
and now that I'm not attached to it

00:05:16.417 --> 00:05:19.005
it's like I can just be like the cat.

00:05:19.005 --> 00:05:20.441
You know I can just go about my business

00:05:20.441 --> 00:05:23.357
and just let it follow
after me wherever I go.

00:05:23.357 --> 00:05:27.252
So what I say to people
who really want to access

00:05:27.252 --> 00:05:29.669
the transition from you know,

00:05:30.817 --> 00:05:32.258
from ambition to meaning,

00:05:32.258 --> 00:05:33.856
if they really want to access it,

00:05:33.856 --> 00:05:36.682
is to get your thoughts off of yourself.

00:05:36.682 --> 00:05:38.691
I do it on the radio every Monday

00:05:38.691 --> 00:05:40.794
when it's like all my questions,

00:05:40.794 --> 00:05:42.149
all the questions are about,

00:05:42.149 --> 00:05:44.138
why can't I manifest this,
why can't I have that,

00:05:44.138 --> 00:05:45.693
this isn't working and so on,

00:05:45.693 --> 00:05:47.738
and my response back to them all the time,

00:05:47.738 --> 00:05:50.604
over and over again, is take what it is

00:05:50.604 --> 00:05:52.871
that you would really like
to attract into your life,

00:05:52.871 --> 00:05:55.208
whatever it is, whether
it's wealth, a job,

00:05:55.208 --> 00:05:57.610
you know know, money, a
nice watch, a new car,

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:01.011
whatever it is and want it more

00:06:01.011 --> 00:06:03.807
for somebody else than
you want it for yourself,

00:06:03.807 --> 00:06:06.891
just it more, just think about that

00:06:06.891 --> 00:06:10.044
and think about how much
joy it would give you

00:06:10.044 --> 00:06:12.825
to be able to put your attention on that

00:06:12.825 --> 00:06:14.970
and just keep your thoughts on that,

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:17.105
you know take your
thoughts off of yourself

00:06:17.105 --> 00:06:19.104
and start living the four virtues.

00:06:19.104 --> 00:06:21.851
Start being sincere,
start being supportive,

00:06:21.851 --> 00:06:25.361
you know start having this
reverence for their life

00:06:25.361 --> 00:06:27.365
and so on and just shift

00:06:27.365 --> 00:06:30.519
off of what's in it for me, you know

00:06:30.519 --> 00:06:32.158
and how much am I going to get

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.765
and why isn't it here fast enough

00:06:33.765 --> 00:06:36.466
and why is theirs shinier than mine?

00:06:36.466 --> 00:06:37.577
And you know and so on.

00:06:37.577 --> 00:06:40.487
Off of that and begin to project that

00:06:40.487 --> 00:06:42.784
and do that, I don't care
whether you're a school teacher,

00:06:42.784 --> 00:06:44.839
I don't care if you're a dental hygienist,

00:06:44.839 --> 00:06:47.709
or if you're a carpenter
or you know whatever it is

00:06:47.709 --> 00:06:49.347
out there that you are doing.

00:06:49.347 --> 00:06:50.910
If you can take your attention,

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.838
if you want the door to open,

00:06:52.838 --> 00:06:55.132
if you want the door to open to meaning

00:06:55.132 --> 00:06:58.432
then the only way that
door is going to open

00:06:58.432 --> 00:07:01.388
is if you understand that you
have to leave your attachment

00:07:01.388 --> 00:07:04.576
to this grossly world
of the material things

00:07:04.576 --> 00:07:06.673
and what's in it for me
and how much am I getting?

00:07:06.673 --> 00:07:11.569
And shift your energy, your
thoughts onto how may I offer,

00:07:11.569 --> 00:07:12.927
how may I serve?

00:07:12.927 --> 00:07:15.998
And I just di a public television special,

00:07:15.998 --> 00:07:17.967
another public television special,

00:07:17.967 --> 00:07:21.932
and an hour-and-a-half
before the show to start

00:07:21.932 --> 00:07:24.510
I was in like one of these
attacks again, in the neck,

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.000
and I was just like you know,

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.281
how am I going to get
through this thing and so on?

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:31.288
And I said a prayer, my wife was there,

00:07:31.288 --> 00:07:33.212
two of my girls were
there, we were in the room,

00:07:33.212 --> 00:07:34.644
I had my arms around them and I said,

00:07:34.644 --> 00:07:37.186
"If I'm supposed to endure this pain,"

00:07:37.186 --> 00:07:39.459
"for whatever reason that
I don't even understand yet

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:40.896
"I'm willing to do it,

00:07:40.896 --> 00:07:43.955
"but could I please just
have the next couple of hours

00:07:43.955 --> 00:07:47.564
"so that I could at least
get through this experience?"

00:07:47.564 --> 00:07:49.751
and it just dissolved, I was able,

00:07:49.751 --> 00:07:51.143
you were there, you were in the audience.

00:07:51.143 --> 00:07:52.986
And I was able to go out there and do it

00:07:52.986 --> 00:07:54.950
and then the pain returned the next day

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.420
and I went right back to that state

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:58.965
and I still do it now and
I can feel it even now

00:07:58.965 --> 00:08:00.924
as we're talking about
it a little bit here

00:08:00.924 --> 00:08:03.754
and instead of cursing it,
instead of being angry at it,

00:08:03.754 --> 00:08:06.944
I accept it as my
dharma, this is you know,

00:08:06.944 --> 00:08:08.837
whatever it is that I
have to learn from it,

00:08:08.837 --> 00:08:13.392
generally speaking every
difficulty I've had in my life,

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:16.142
getting divorced, literally being

00:08:17.792 --> 00:08:19.430
someone who is addicted

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:22.303
to substances, including alcohol.

00:08:22.303 --> 00:08:26.053
Letting go of you know
those kinds of beliefs

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:29.217
that those are terrible things
that I should be ashamed of,

00:08:29.217 --> 00:08:31.510
they've been amongst my greatest teachers

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.550
and this pain is just
another one of those things

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:36.535
and generally speaking I now
can go out and help people

00:08:36.535 --> 00:08:38.748
who live in chronic pain
and you do a lot of this

00:08:38.748 --> 00:08:40.136
with your training.

00:08:40.136 --> 00:08:42.057
You know I've seen you do it on stage,

00:08:42.057 --> 00:08:43.042
you know with people,

00:08:43.042 --> 00:08:44.700
in fact when we were out in Australia,

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:45.929
that one women, what was it?

00:08:45.929 --> 00:08:46.993
She couldn't even?

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:48.536
- Well there was one lady
with a frozen shoulder.

00:08:48.536 --> 00:08:49.369
- Right.

00:08:49.369 --> 00:08:50.202
- Couldn't move here arm.

00:08:50.202 --> 00:08:51.206
- Hadn't been able to
move her arm in years.

00:08:51.206 --> 00:08:52.039
- In a year and in 20 minutes

00:08:52.039 --> 00:08:53.098
she got it up like that.

00:08:53.098 --> 00:08:53.931
- Yeah.

00:08:53.931 --> 00:08:56.966
So it's like and that comes
from just accepting yourself

00:08:56.966 --> 00:08:59.096
and actually instead of cursing the pain

00:08:59.096 --> 00:09:02.163
because when you curse the
pain and get angry at it

00:09:02.163 --> 00:09:04.828
you just, you get angry at
every cell of your being

00:09:04.828 --> 00:09:06.262
goes through that same anger

00:09:06.262 --> 00:09:07.692
and what you want to do is

00:09:07.692 --> 00:09:09.779
just get to that peaceful
place within yourself

00:09:09.779 --> 00:09:12.173
where you say, you know,
when you trust in yourself,

00:09:12.173 --> 00:09:14.148
when you trust in yourself

00:09:14.148 --> 00:09:16.819
you're really trusting in
the wisdom that created you,

00:09:16.819 --> 00:09:17.652
you know.

00:09:17.652 --> 00:09:20.415
And the wisdom that
created you is infinite.

00:09:20.415 --> 00:09:23.201
And it's formless, so your thoughts

00:09:23.201 --> 00:09:25.105
are in that same category,

00:09:25.105 --> 00:09:29.161
have thoughts that aligned
with that divine presence.

00:09:29.161 --> 00:09:29.994
- Yeah.

00:09:29.994 --> 00:09:31.006
- You'll see it going away.

00:09:31.006 --> 00:09:33.756
The obscure outlasts the obvious,

00:09:34.811 --> 00:09:37.441
try to become a little more obscure,

00:09:37.441 --> 00:09:39.364
a little less interfering,

00:09:39.364 --> 00:09:41.528
a little less, notice me.

00:09:41.528 --> 00:09:44.267
A little less, you know one of
the specific kinds of things

00:09:44.267 --> 00:09:46.507
that you can do is just as you're about,

00:09:46.507 --> 00:09:48.000
when somebody else is talking,

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.173
just as you're about to interject

00:09:50.173 --> 00:09:52.104
what you've been thinking
about for the whole time

00:09:52.104 --> 00:09:53.666
waiting for them to stop talking,

00:09:53.666 --> 00:09:54.499
(audience laughing)

00:09:54.499 --> 00:09:56.612
to just stop, to bite your tongue

00:09:56.612 --> 00:10:00.118
and say tell me more or
that's very interesting

00:10:00.118 --> 00:10:02.087
I have never heard that
point of view before.

00:10:02.087 --> 00:10:04.262
Even if they totally, completely disagree

00:10:04.262 --> 00:10:06.391
with everything that you stand for

00:10:06.391 --> 00:10:09.972
to be willing to listen, to
be able to stop, practice it.

00:10:09.972 --> 00:10:12.594
I practiced it when I
did the verses of the Tao

00:10:12.594 --> 00:10:16.656
I practiced it every single day
while I was working on that.

00:10:16.656 --> 00:10:20.548
Just staying obscure and for
me that's not always so easy

00:10:20.548 --> 00:10:23.165
because of just being
recognized wherever I go.

00:10:23.165 --> 00:10:25.619
And if I saw someone who
was about to recognize me

00:10:25.619 --> 00:10:26.970
I would just put my head down,

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:29.201
I would just walk a little bit
past them, like I'm saying,

00:10:29.201 --> 00:10:31.616
right now I just want to be anonymous.

00:10:31.616 --> 00:10:33.907
Right now I want to be obscure.

00:10:33.907 --> 00:10:35.710
All things are possible

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:36.979
and I always ask an audience

00:10:36.979 --> 00:10:38.654
what does that leave out?

00:10:38.654 --> 00:10:40.754
You know, that all things are possible

00:10:40.754 --> 00:10:42.689
literally means all things are possible.

00:10:42.689 --> 00:10:46.013
So whatever it is you'd like
to attract into your life,

00:10:46.013 --> 00:10:47.560
whatever it is you'd like to accomplish,

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:49.120
whatever you'd like to do in your life,

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.438
if you start from a spiritual place,

00:10:51.438 --> 00:10:53.206
a place of all things are possible

00:10:53.206 --> 00:10:55.663
if I return and you know
and get to that place.

00:10:55.663 --> 00:10:57.215
And then I begin to visualize it.

00:10:57.215 --> 00:10:58.972
And then I begin to use my imagination

00:10:58.972 --> 00:11:01.151
because everything that we see around us,

00:11:01.151 --> 00:11:02.666
everything in this world

00:11:02.666 --> 00:11:04.516
was once imagined, every thing.

00:11:04.516 --> 00:11:06.154
You know that camera that is there,

00:11:06.154 --> 00:11:07.463
the clothes that you're wearing,

00:11:07.463 --> 00:11:08.815
the chairs that we're sitting on.

00:11:08.815 --> 00:11:11.564
Every thing once had to be imagined.

00:11:11.564 --> 00:11:14.195
If you get that, I mean
Einstein's famous observation

00:11:14.195 --> 00:11:17.383
was that imagination's more
important than knowledge.

00:11:17.383 --> 00:11:19.676
If you can learn how
important your imagination is

00:11:19.676 --> 00:11:22.089
and that's where you're
spirit is, in that place

00:11:22.089 --> 00:11:24.546
and then once you go to that place

00:11:24.546 --> 00:11:26.602
in what it is you'd like
to attract into your life,

00:11:26.602 --> 00:11:28.672
you're coming from a spiritual place,

00:11:28.672 --> 00:11:30.677
absolutely nothing is impossible.

00:11:30.677 --> 00:11:32.025
It was Thomas Troward,

00:11:32.025 --> 00:11:34.323
he did some lectures on mental science

00:11:34.323 --> 00:11:36.573
way back in the 1907, 1908.

00:11:37.469 --> 00:11:38.900
He was from Scotland

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.069
He was from Scotland, and one
of the things that he said,

00:11:41.069 --> 00:11:43.281
is that the law of flotation

00:11:43.281 --> 00:11:45.910
was not discovered by the contemplation

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:47.993
of the sinking of things.

00:11:50.239 --> 00:11:53.975
So that like before the
15th and 16th centuries

00:11:53.975 --> 00:11:56.926
all of the ships were made out of wood.

00:11:56.926 --> 00:11:59.507
Not because iron wasn't available

00:11:59.507 --> 00:12:00.900
and steel wasn't available,

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:04.740
but because there was a
belief that wood floated

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.872
so therefore you had to make ships

00:12:06.872 --> 00:12:10.312
out of things that floated,
that's literally how the,

00:12:10.312 --> 00:12:11.583
and then someone came along and said,

00:12:11.583 --> 00:12:13.099
that it has absolutely nothing to do

00:12:13.099 --> 00:12:14.696
with what things are made out of

00:12:14.696 --> 00:12:15.968
it has to do with the amount of water

00:12:15.968 --> 00:12:17.478
that is being dispersed.

00:12:17.478 --> 00:12:20.217
That's what determines whether
something will float or not.

00:12:20.217 --> 00:12:21.818
And I think about that all the time

00:12:21.818 --> 00:12:25.880
because it's in the
contemplation of what you desire

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:27.763
that you create what it is that you want

00:12:27.763 --> 00:12:28.833
to have for yourself,

00:12:28.833 --> 00:12:31.529
it's in your willingness to contemplate it

00:12:31.529 --> 00:12:34.151
and nothing more according to Troward

00:12:34.151 --> 00:12:35.956
and mental science.

00:12:35.956 --> 00:12:38.327
So then I think about the Wright brothers,

00:12:38.327 --> 00:12:40.044
you know 100 or so years ago,

00:12:40.044 --> 00:12:42.977
and I said the law of
flying was not discovered by

00:12:42.977 --> 00:12:46.044
the contemplation of the
staying on the ground of things.

00:12:46.044 --> 00:12:47.928
So that these were two people,

00:12:47.928 --> 00:12:50.216
like for me to figure out
how to get an airplane to fly

00:12:50.216 --> 00:12:52.189
and my limited knowledge of all that

00:12:52.189 --> 00:12:53.671
I would probably have contemplated

00:12:53.671 --> 00:12:55.431
the staying on the ground of things.

00:12:55.431 --> 00:12:57.024
You know like this is what happens,

00:12:57.024 --> 00:12:58.709
but there's somebody came along

00:12:58.709 --> 00:13:00.887
and contemplated the idea that

00:13:00.887 --> 00:13:02.157
if you get enough speed going

00:13:02.157 --> 00:13:03.387
and you have the right design

00:13:03.387 --> 00:13:05.528
and you get pressure
underneath something like this

00:13:05.528 --> 00:13:08.353
that this thing is going
to lift up off the earth,

00:13:08.353 --> 00:13:10.277
somebody had to contemplate that idea.

00:13:10.277 --> 00:13:13.017
And everybody who contemplated
that it wasn't possible,

00:13:13.017 --> 00:13:15.214
that it couldn't work was a part

00:13:15.214 --> 00:13:17.102
of why flying didn't take place

00:13:17.102 --> 00:13:19.117
because there was no new law discovered

00:13:19.117 --> 00:13:21.455
in the early part of the 20th century,

00:13:21.455 --> 00:13:25.429
anymore than electricity was
discovered by Thomas Edison

00:13:25.429 --> 00:13:26.819
or anyone like that,

00:13:26.819 --> 00:13:28.335
I mean the ability to have electricity

00:13:28.335 --> 00:13:31.748
has always been there,
somebody has to contemplate.

00:13:31.748 --> 00:13:33.800
So it's like in your own personal life

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:35.854
your willingness to contemplate yourself

00:13:35.854 --> 00:13:38.399
as a person who is capable
of attracting into your life

00:13:38.399 --> 00:13:39.350
what you want,

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:41.332
having the kind of
relationships that you want,

00:13:41.332 --> 00:13:42.902
being able to have abundance

00:13:42.902 --> 00:13:45.104
where you know scarcity always existed,

00:13:45.104 --> 00:13:47.036
all you have to do is begin the process

00:13:47.036 --> 00:13:49.491
by being willing to contemplate

00:13:49.491 --> 00:13:51.783
the presence of that in your life.

00:13:51.783 --> 00:13:52.935
And I've always been a person

00:13:52.935 --> 00:13:54.901
that I can remember throughout my life

00:13:54.901 --> 00:13:56.946
as someone who could contemplate myself

00:13:56.946 --> 00:13:59.603
being able to do things
that most people couldn't

00:13:59.603 --> 00:14:01.003
and I can give you a good example.

00:14:01.003 --> 00:14:03.343
When my mother got us all back together

00:14:03.343 --> 00:14:05.804
and we were living in Detroit,
on the east side of Detroit,

00:14:05.804 --> 00:14:07.535
and we got a new television set.

00:14:07.535 --> 00:14:09.840
It was a black-and-white, it
was a screen about this big,

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:11.186
it was an Admiral

00:14:11.186 --> 00:14:13.134
and we had it in our home and it was like,

00:14:13.134 --> 00:14:15.101
oh, black-and-white television, you know,

00:14:15.101 --> 00:14:17.268
you remember Uncle Miltie?

00:14:19.803 --> 00:14:23.410
There was a guy that was on
TV, his name was Steve Allen,

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.990
and he was on The Tonight Show.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:30.090
I was 11, 12, 13 years
old, I was born in 1940

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.594
so it was '51 or '52,

00:14:32.594 --> 00:14:34.230
and I used to stay up
every night and watch

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:35.463
The Tonight Show,

00:14:35.463 --> 00:14:38.454
even though I had to go
to school the next day

00:14:38.454 --> 00:14:40.912
there was just something about that show,

00:14:40.912 --> 00:14:42.308
you know and all of the characters,

00:14:42.308 --> 00:14:45.593
the Spock Mock, and all the
things that Steve Allen would do

00:14:45.593 --> 00:14:48.655
and I would come down when I
would be talking the next day

00:14:48.655 --> 00:14:52.666
and I would be telling my
mother and my two brothers,

00:14:52.666 --> 00:14:55.369
that when I do The Tonight Show,

00:14:55.369 --> 00:14:58.026
this is what I would
say, I wouldn't have said

00:14:58.026 --> 00:15:00.406
what Louis Nye said, how he reacted,

00:15:00.406 --> 00:15:03.522
I would have said, and I used to do this

00:15:03.522 --> 00:15:05.541
and my brothers and my mother would say,

00:15:05.541 --> 00:15:07.427
that's just Wayne, he's just nutty,

00:15:07.427 --> 00:15:09.282
he thinks he's on The Tonight Show,

00:15:09.282 --> 00:15:10.115
(laughing)

00:15:10.115 --> 00:15:11.591
he thinks he's going
to do The Tonight Show

00:15:11.591 --> 00:15:13.861
and I would go up into my room

00:15:13.861 --> 00:15:16.154
in this little tiny
house that we lived in,

00:15:16.154 --> 00:15:18.037
a little two bedroom house

00:15:18.037 --> 00:15:20.981
that five of us lived in
because my mother remarried

00:15:20.981 --> 00:15:24.629
and I would see myself
doing The Tonight Show,

00:15:24.629 --> 00:15:27.812
I would just practice it and
Steve Allen became someone

00:15:27.812 --> 00:15:29.770
that I was really enamored with.

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:31.776
Well you know fast forward,

00:15:31.776 --> 00:15:34.532
I don't know, 30 years or whatever or so,

00:15:34.532 --> 00:15:37.729
and I've written a book
Your Erroneous Zones,

00:15:37.729 --> 00:15:39.565
The Tonight Show calls and they ask me

00:15:39.565 --> 00:15:41.082
if I would like to come on and do it,

00:15:41.082 --> 00:15:43.628
so I do my first stint
on The Tonight Show,

00:15:43.628 --> 00:15:46.055
I did the show like 37 times

00:15:46.055 --> 00:15:48.142
over a period of three or four years

00:15:48.142 --> 00:15:49.407
with all these different hosts,

00:15:49.407 --> 00:15:51.412
but Johnny Carson was on,

00:15:51.412 --> 00:15:53.888
and the first guest on the very first show

00:15:53.888 --> 00:15:57.471
when I did the show was Steve Allen.

00:15:57.471 --> 00:15:59.189
And it was like something clicked in me

00:15:59.189 --> 00:16:01.483
that I had contemplated that as a child

00:16:01.483 --> 00:16:03.077
I had always had a knowing

00:16:03.077 --> 00:16:05.791
and I can remember sitting
there talking to Johnny

00:16:05.791 --> 00:16:08.099
about this thing that, you know,

00:16:08.099 --> 00:16:09.775
and Steve Allen was sitting
there right next to me

00:16:09.775 --> 00:16:11.376
and we were talking about that kind of.

00:16:11.376 --> 00:16:13.505
So by putting my attention on something,

00:16:13.505 --> 00:16:16.424
it wasn't some deliberate
thing that I was doing

00:16:16.424 --> 00:16:18.190
you know when I was 11 or 12 years old

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:20.225
that was designating
that I was going to be

00:16:20.225 --> 00:16:23.292
a person who was going to
be appearing on talk shows

00:16:23.292 --> 00:16:25.915
30 years from now, it
was just an awareness,

00:16:25.915 --> 00:16:28.176
a willingness to contemplate,

00:16:28.176 --> 00:16:31.613
to contemplate myself
in that kind of a place.

00:16:31.613 --> 00:16:33.699
And I think the power of contemplation

00:16:33.699 --> 00:16:36.152
is the thing that most
people haven't harnessed yet.

00:16:36.152 --> 00:16:38.741
And when you harness it in your life

00:16:38.741 --> 00:16:39.852
there's absolutely no limit

00:16:39.852 --> 00:16:41.291
to what you can attract into your life,

00:16:41.291 --> 00:16:43.862
if you absolutely stay
focused on what it is

00:16:43.862 --> 00:16:46.402
that you know you're going
to manifest and attract,

00:16:46.402 --> 00:16:49.141
you're not going to do it in your time,

00:16:49.141 --> 00:16:50.817
you know Jackson Browne
sings a song that says,

00:16:50.817 --> 00:16:54.110
let creation reveal its secrets by and by.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:55.472
I mean you can't push the river,

00:16:55.472 --> 00:16:57.960
you can't, it's all done in divine time,

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:00.665
but it will show, it will show.

00:17:00.665 --> 00:17:03.865
It will manifest, it will attract itself

00:17:03.865 --> 00:17:06.578
and I'm never surprised any longer

00:17:06.578 --> 00:17:08.791
about anything that I put my thoughts on

00:17:08.791 --> 00:17:10.548
that I can attract it into my life.

00:17:10.548 --> 00:17:12.426
I just absolutely know
that law of attraction

00:17:12.426 --> 00:17:14.725
and that it absolutely works.

00:17:14.725 --> 00:17:17.392
Giving up your personal history.

00:17:18.985 --> 00:17:23.066
And I learned it from a
man named Carlos Castaneda

00:17:23.066 --> 00:17:26.131
who once said that one day he said,

00:17:26.131 --> 00:17:29.101
"I finally realized
that I no longer needed

00:17:29.101 --> 00:17:30.768
"a personal history.

00:17:31.737 --> 00:17:33.427
"and just like drinking" he said,

00:17:33.427 --> 00:17:36.140
"I gave it up and that and only that

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:39.466
"has made all the
difference in the world."

00:17:39.466 --> 00:17:40.648
You know the nice thing

00:17:40.648 --> 00:17:42.743
about giving up your personal history?

00:17:42.743 --> 00:17:45.213
Is that if you don't have a story

00:17:45.213 --> 00:17:47.628
you don't have to live up to it.

00:17:47.628 --> 00:17:50.122
(audience laughing)

00:17:50.122 --> 00:17:52.916
All of us have these bags

00:17:52.916 --> 00:17:55.353
of manure that we carry around with us

00:17:55.353 --> 00:17:56.520
called our past

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:58.764
and the people who have done things to us

00:17:58.764 --> 00:18:00.328
and the events and the circumstances,

00:18:00.328 --> 00:18:03.694
all of this stuff that
we use and we bond to

00:18:03.694 --> 00:18:05.939
and we bond ourself to
these wounds of our past

00:18:05.939 --> 00:18:08.864
and we identify ourself on
the basis of these wounds

00:18:08.864 --> 00:18:10.471
and every once in a while we set it down

00:18:10.471 --> 00:18:12.928
and we reach in there and we
smear it all over ourselves.

00:18:12.928 --> 00:18:13.761
(audience laughing)

00:18:13.761 --> 00:18:15.835
And then we wonder why
does my life smell so bad?

00:18:15.835 --> 00:18:17.222
I don't understand this?

00:18:17.222 --> 00:18:18.411
(audience laughing)

00:18:18.411 --> 00:18:21.781
When in fact the now, this moment,

00:18:21.781 --> 00:18:23.848
merging yourself into the now

00:18:23.848 --> 00:18:26.585
means that you may have
been in a relationship,

00:18:26.585 --> 00:18:29.537
I had a woman from Holland
who came over to see me,

00:18:29.537 --> 00:18:32.256
whose husband had left her after 25 years,

00:18:32.256 --> 00:18:33.777
she had four children

00:18:33.777 --> 00:18:36.433
and she just had been
on the verge of suicide.

00:18:36.433 --> 00:18:38.974
And she was loosing weight
and she was depressed

00:18:38.974 --> 00:18:41.321
and she was taking all
kinds of drugs for it

00:18:41.321 --> 00:18:43.044
and she was getting sicker and sicker

00:18:43.044 --> 00:18:45.388
because she just couldn't get over it.

00:18:45.388 --> 00:18:47.901
And she came to a book
signing that I was doing

00:18:47.901 --> 00:18:50.234
at a bookstore down in Florida

00:18:50.234 --> 00:18:53.366
and she said, "You've got
to say something to me.

00:18:53.366 --> 00:18:56.082
"You've got to say something to me,

00:18:56.082 --> 00:18:59.189
"that will help me to get over this."

00:18:59.189 --> 00:19:02.261
and I told her this line, I said,

00:19:02.261 --> 00:19:04.710
"Give up your personal history,

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:08.391
"merge yourself here,
now into this moment."

00:19:08.391 --> 00:19:10.271
and those 25 years are something,

00:19:10.271 --> 00:19:12.700
if you want to understand how to do it

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:14.450
think of your past as

00:19:16.563 --> 00:19:17.646
oh, this hat"

00:19:18.661 --> 00:19:20.390
and this is your past,

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:23.906
now you can't just set
this thing down over here

00:19:23.906 --> 00:19:26.954
and walk away from it and
give up your personal history

00:19:26.954 --> 00:19:31.216
because you will always have
it there to look back at.

00:19:31.216 --> 00:19:34.216
What you do is you pick up your past

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:40.545
and you embrace, you
understand it, you accept it

00:19:40.545 --> 00:19:43.820
as I had to go through these
things that I had to go through

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:46.316
in order for me to get to this place today

00:19:46.316 --> 00:19:48.904
and the evidence for that is that I did.

00:19:48.904 --> 00:19:51.120
You don't need anymore evidence,

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:51.980
you did.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:53.730
And then you toss it,

00:19:55.502 --> 00:19:56.782
you toss it,

00:19:56.782 --> 00:19:59.524
you embrace it, and you toss it

00:19:59.524 --> 00:20:02.226
and you merge into the now

00:20:02.226 --> 00:20:04.652
by giving up your attachment.

00:20:04.652 --> 00:20:06.490
And some of you have
heard me use the metaphor

00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:09.517
of the wake, Alan Watts
talked about the wake

00:20:09.517 --> 00:20:11.188
is not what drives the boat,

00:20:11.188 --> 00:20:13.832
the wake is just a trail
that is left behind,

00:20:13.832 --> 00:20:14.990
that's all it is

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:17.131
and so is the wake of your life

00:20:17.131 --> 00:20:19.384
and the wake doesn't make the boat go

00:20:19.384 --> 00:20:21.190
and neither does the wake of your life,

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:22.289
the reason why your life

00:20:22.289 --> 00:20:24.337
is going in the direction that it is,

00:20:24.337 --> 00:20:26.763
the wake is a trail that is left behind

00:20:26.763 --> 00:20:29.082
and it's an illusion to believe

00:20:29.082 --> 00:20:31.626
that it is the cause of your suffering

00:20:31.626 --> 00:20:34.003
or your struggles or your difficulty,

00:20:34.003 --> 00:20:35.724
give it up, let it go,

00:20:35.724 --> 00:20:39.660
embrace it, understand it, get
help doing that if you must,

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:41.516
and then move into the now.

00:20:41.516 --> 00:20:45.663
Thinking small is what
gets great things done,

00:20:45.663 --> 00:20:47.123
Verse 63.

00:20:47.123 --> 00:20:50.042
Achieve greatness in little things.

00:20:50.042 --> 00:20:54.030
Take on difficulties
while they are still easy.

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:57.558
Do great things while
they are still small.

00:20:57.558 --> 00:21:01.483
The sage, the sage, one
of my daughter's names,

00:21:01.483 --> 00:21:05.020
does not attempt anything very big

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:07.353
and thus achieves greatness.

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:12.356
Greatness comes from being in the moment,

00:21:12.356 --> 00:21:14.439
here, present in the now.

00:21:15.724 --> 00:21:18.307
The sage confronts difficulties

00:21:19.205 --> 00:21:21.455
but never experiences them.

00:21:22.439 --> 00:21:25.272
This is the idea of thinking small

00:21:27.045 --> 00:21:31.390
and finally, I'd like to see
you change from this thought.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:35.234
Change from seeing yourself as separate

00:21:35.234 --> 00:21:38.927
to seeing yourself as
connected to everyone

00:21:38.927 --> 00:21:41.800
and everything in the universe.

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:43.481
I sat and read an essay

00:21:43.481 --> 00:21:46.980
called The Whole Man by Abraham Maslow,

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:49.897
and Maslow was the first
person that I'd ever seen

00:21:49.897 --> 00:21:52.337
in the field of psychology who spoke about

00:21:52.337 --> 00:21:55.324
we should not be assessing
who human beings are

00:21:55.324 --> 00:21:58.318
and what they're capable of
doing based upon what's missing

00:21:58.318 --> 00:22:01.216
or what's wrong or what they
can't do or their weaknesses,

00:22:01.216 --> 00:22:05.280
we shouldn't study neurology,
neurological disorders,

00:22:05.280 --> 00:22:08.732
we shouldn't study how
psychotic people are

00:22:08.732 --> 00:22:10.369
or how neurotic they are.

00:22:10.369 --> 00:22:12.479
We should look at the greatest achievers

00:22:12.479 --> 00:22:13.993
who've ever walked among us,

00:22:13.993 --> 00:22:16.447
know that they all came
from the same intelligence

00:22:16.447 --> 00:22:19.031
and recognize and help people to find that

00:22:19.031 --> 00:22:20.531
within themselves.

00:22:21.374 --> 00:22:23.667
And I read this essay I was so taken by it

00:22:23.667 --> 00:22:26.782
and he talked about the
qualities or the characteristics

00:22:26.782 --> 00:22:30.139
of what he called self-actualizing people.

00:22:30.139 --> 00:22:32.580
And he said the number one
quality and characteristic

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:34.924
of these people who live at the apex

00:22:34.924 --> 00:22:36.730
of what he called self-actualization

00:22:36.730 --> 00:22:38.817
who are way beyond just taking care

00:22:38.817 --> 00:22:40.536
of their biological needs,

00:22:40.536 --> 00:22:43.454
who are way beyond their social needs,

00:22:43.454 --> 00:22:46.122
who are way beyond needing
to be loved and so on,

00:22:46.122 --> 00:22:48.711
these are people who
came here with a purpose.

00:22:48.711 --> 00:22:50.514
These are people who have a dharma,

00:22:50.514 --> 00:22:52.368
these are people who won't let anyone else

00:22:52.368 --> 00:22:54.703
determine what it is they're going to be.

00:22:54.703 --> 00:22:57.121
He said the number one
quality of these people

00:22:57.121 --> 00:22:58.616
is that they are independent

00:22:58.616 --> 00:23:00.871
of the good opinion of other people.

00:23:00.871 --> 00:23:02.585
They listen to an inner voice.

00:23:02.585 --> 00:23:05.364
Yes, our physical body is what it is

00:23:05.364 --> 00:23:07.018
but we can make choices about it.

00:23:07.018 --> 00:23:11.007
Yes, our spiritual body,
our purpose, our dharma,

00:23:11.007 --> 00:23:13.955
what we're here for is also doomed,

00:23:13.955 --> 00:23:16.407
but we makes choices,
what are the choices?

00:23:16.407 --> 00:23:18.780
You came here to be a great artist,

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:22.379
I did a whole film on
this, it's called The Shift

00:23:22.379 --> 00:23:25.399
and this whole idea is that

00:23:25.399 --> 00:23:27.609
you came here to be a great artist,

00:23:27.609 --> 00:23:30.518
do you pick up a paint brush?

00:23:30.518 --> 00:23:34.337
Do you do what van Gogh did
you just go out there and paint

00:23:34.337 --> 00:23:35.974
because it's in your soul,

00:23:35.974 --> 00:23:38.221
because the second characteristic

00:23:38.221 --> 00:23:40.719
of self-actualizing
people according to Maslow

00:23:40.719 --> 00:23:43.838
is that they are detached from outcome,

00:23:43.838 --> 00:23:46.671
they don't do what they do because

00:23:47.848 --> 00:23:51.260
of what result is going to come to them,

00:23:51.260 --> 00:23:52.945
because of how much money
they're going to make,

00:23:52.945 --> 00:23:54.341
how much prestige they're going to get,

00:23:54.341 --> 00:23:56.071
how big their business is going to grow,

00:23:56.071 --> 00:23:59.423
that is not what motivates
self-actualized people.

00:23:59.423 --> 00:24:03.617
What motivates self-actualizing people is

00:24:03.617 --> 00:24:05.200
this is my calling,

00:24:07.187 --> 00:24:11.366
I found myself reading the
Bhagavad Gita for the third time

00:24:11.366 --> 00:24:13.473
in the last three months,

00:24:13.473 --> 00:24:14.956
I just keep reading it over and over,

00:24:14.956 --> 00:24:17.171
just like when I did the Tao,

00:24:17.171 --> 00:24:19.795
eight years ago when I turned 65,

00:24:19.795 --> 00:24:22.263
and couldn't stop it

00:24:22.263 --> 00:24:24.446
and the teachers showed up.

00:24:24.446 --> 00:24:27.536
The Buddhist proverb is that
when the student is ready

00:24:27.536 --> 00:24:29.053
the teachers will appear.

00:24:29.053 --> 00:24:30.645
It's not whether there's teachers there,

00:24:30.645 --> 00:24:33.135
there's teachers everywhere.

00:24:33.135 --> 00:24:35.113
Everything is a teaching,

00:24:35.113 --> 00:24:37.414
the question isn't whether
the teachers are there,

00:24:37.414 --> 00:24:40.708
the question is how willing are you

00:24:40.708 --> 00:24:42.593
to pay attention?

00:24:42.593 --> 00:24:45.176
How willing are you to
listen to that inner voice

00:24:45.176 --> 00:24:47.600
that no one else can hear?

00:24:47.600 --> 00:24:49.114
That little scurvy elephant in there

00:24:49.114 --> 00:24:52.197
that says, you're not the boss of me,

00:24:53.594 --> 00:24:56.594
you can't tell me what I'm here for.

00:24:58.099 --> 00:25:00.933
It takes a kind of fearlessness

00:25:00.933 --> 00:25:05.216
because fear is such a
omnipresent force in our lives.

00:25:05.216 --> 00:25:09.563
I do what I do because
of the passion I feel,

00:25:09.563 --> 00:25:12.981
I am not here because of what
you paid me to be here for.

00:25:12.981 --> 00:25:15.967
I am not here because of any need

00:25:15.967 --> 00:25:17.850
that I have to sell another book,

00:25:17.850 --> 00:25:21.009
I am not here for anything
external to myself.

00:25:21.009 --> 00:25:24.759
I am here because I have
a passion within me.

00:25:27.145 --> 00:25:29.250
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:25:29.250 --> 00:25:32.035
I made this video because
Ibby Hadeed asked me to.

00:25:32.035 --> 00:25:33.427
Also if you want to nominate someone

00:25:33.427 --> 00:25:34.823
for the next Top 10 Video

00:25:34.823 --> 00:25:37.362
please check the description
for a link to a video

00:25:37.362 --> 00:25:38.804
where you can vote for people

00:25:38.804 --> 00:25:40.726
and put it in your suggestions as well.

00:25:40.726 --> 00:25:42.941
I'd love to know what'd
you take from this video?

00:25:42.941 --> 00:25:44.992
What was the most important lesson

00:25:44.992 --> 00:25:47.083
that you learned that blew your mind

00:25:47.083 --> 00:25:49.132
that you're going to immediately apply

00:25:49.132 --> 00:25:51.140
to your life or your business somehow?

00:25:51.140 --> 00:25:52.818
Please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:25:52.818 --> 00:25:54.209
I'm super curious to find out.

00:25:54.209 --> 00:25:55.851
I also want to give a quick shout-out

00:25:55.851 --> 00:25:58.551
to Dave Gardner, from thedavidgardner.com,

00:25:58.551 --> 00:26:00.817
Dave thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:26:00.817 --> 00:26:01.685
Your One Word,

00:26:01.685 --> 00:26:03.688
taking that picture, sending it in,

00:26:03.688 --> 00:26:05.652
I really, really appreciate
your support, man,

00:26:05.652 --> 00:26:07.008
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:26:07.008 --> 00:26:08.645
So thank you guys again, for watching.

00:26:08.645 --> 00:26:09.835
I believe in you,

00:26:09.835 --> 00:26:11.903
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:26:11.903 --> 00:26:14.146
and whatever your one word is,

00:26:14.146 --> 00:26:16.563
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:26:22.493 --> 00:26:25.333
- The ego is not worth defending.

00:26:25.333 --> 00:26:27.598
And we all spend a lot of our time

00:26:27.598 --> 00:26:29.612
defending this thing that says,

00:26:29.612 --> 00:26:31.289
well you know I am what I do have

00:26:31.289 --> 00:26:32.398
and I have to get more things

00:26:32.398 --> 00:26:33.704
and if I don't have as much as they do

00:26:33.704 --> 00:26:34.687
then they're going to,

00:26:34.687 --> 00:26:37.181
and we go through our lives
doing all of this stuff

00:26:37.181 --> 00:26:39.405
and what it does is it
brings us to a point where

00:26:39.405 --> 00:26:42.590
we not longer have something
or our reputation is gone

00:26:42.590 --> 00:26:44.962
or is taken away from
us or somebody steals it

00:26:44.962 --> 00:26:46.109
and what happens to us?

00:26:46.109 --> 00:26:49.794
Or when we retire or no
longer can do things,

00:26:49.794 --> 00:26:51.962
so now people get over a certain age

00:26:51.962 --> 00:26:54.053
and they just feel like,
you know I've declined

00:26:54.053 --> 00:26:55.946
and so, there's nothing in the DNA

00:26:55.946 --> 00:26:58.164
that says you have to
decline ever in your life.

00:26:58.164 --> 00:26:59.188
You don't have to decline,

00:26:59.188 --> 00:27:00.823
your DNA's over 600,000 years old.

00:27:00.823 --> 00:27:01.973
- So then why do we have it though?

00:27:01.973 --> 00:27:02.876
Why do we have it?

00:27:02.876 --> 00:27:04.193
- We have it because it works,

00:27:04.193 --> 00:27:06.994
it works at getting ourselves believing

00:27:06.994 --> 00:27:08.596
that we're better than other people

00:27:08.596 --> 00:27:11.177
instead of just allowing
ourselves to be free

00:27:11.177 --> 00:27:13.046
and that's just like,

00:27:13.046 --> 00:27:16.573
the Tao teaches us to un-peel the onion,

00:27:16.573 --> 00:27:18.495
un-peel layers to get to,

00:27:18.495 --> 00:27:21.254
the essence of the Tao is emptiness,

00:27:21.254 --> 00:27:22.976
getting to that place of emptiness,

00:27:22.976 --> 00:27:25.356
that's like the supreme place to get to.

00:27:25.356 --> 00:27:27.035
Where you're just empty of all of that

00:27:27.035 --> 00:27:27.936
and then you're free,

00:27:27.936 --> 00:27:29.039
and then guess what?

00:27:29.039 --> 00:27:31.417
All of the things that
you wanted so desperately

00:27:31.417 --> 00:27:33.757
when you were so ego dominated before

00:27:33.757 --> 00:27:35.149
begin to show up in your life

00:27:35.149 --> 00:27:37.691
in larger and larger and larger amounts.

